@EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5293

### 1. GET all employees (Success: 200 OK)
GET {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. GET employee by valid ID (Success: 200 OK)
GET {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/1
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. GET employee by non-existent ID (Failure: 404 Not Found)
GET {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/999
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. POST Create Employee - Valid payload (Success: 201 Created)
POST {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Kavitha",
  "email": "kavitha@example.com",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "salary": 65000,
  "joiningDate": "2024-03-01T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 5. POST Create Employee - Invalid payload: Empty name, bad email, invalid salary (Failure: 400 Bad Request)
POST {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "invalid-email-format",
  "department": "A",
  "salary": -500,
  "joiningDate": "2024-03-01T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 6. PUT Update Employee - Valid payload (Success: 204 No Content)
PUT {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Thiru Updated",
  "email": "thiru.updated@example.com",
  "department": "IT Leadership",
  "salary": 55000,
  "joiningDate": "2024-01-15T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 7. PUT Update Employee - Non-existent ID (Failure: 404 Not Found)
PUT {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ghost Employee",
  "email": "ghost@example.com",
  "department": "Finance",
  "salary": 40000,
  "joiningDate": "2024-01-15T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 8. PUT Update Employee - Validation failure (Failure: 400 Bad Request)
PUT {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "T",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "department": "",
  "salary": 50,
  "joiningDate": "2024-01-15T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 9. DELETE Employee - Valid ID (Success: 204 No Content)
DELETE {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/2

###

### 10. DELETE Employee - Non-existent ID (Failure: 404 Not Found)
DELETE {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/999

###

### ── DAY 9: FILTERING, SORTING, PAGINATION & RELATIONSHIPS ─────────────

### 11. GET Paged Employees (Default Page 1, Size 10)
GET {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/paged?page=1&pageSize=5
Accept: application/json

###

### 12. GET Filtered & Sorted Employees (Department filter + Sort by Salary Desc)
GET {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/paged?department=IT&sortBy=salary&isDescending=true
Accept: application/json

###

### 13. GET All Departments with Eager-Loaded Employees
GET {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/department
Accept: application/json

###

### 14. GET Department by ID
GET {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/department/1
Accept: application/json

###

### 15. POST Create Department
POST {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/department
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Data Science & AI",
  "description": "Machine learning and artificial intelligence solutions"
}

###

### ── DAY 10: AUTHENTICATION & AUTHORIZATION (GATE 2) ──────────────────

### 16. Login as Admin (Role: Admin)
# @name adminLogin
POST {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "Admin@123"
}

###

### 17. Login as Standard User (Role: User)
# @name userLogin
POST {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "user",
  "password": "User@123"
}

###

### 18. Unauthenticated Request — Access Protected POST without Token (Expected: 401 Unauthorized)
POST {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Anonymous User",
  "email": "anon@example.com",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "salary": 70000,
  "joiningDate": "2024-04-01T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 19. Authenticated Request — Access Protected POST with Token (Expected: 201 Created)
POST {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

{
  "name": "Authorized Employee",
  "email": "auth.emp@example.com",
  "department": "Engineering",
  "salary": 75000,
  "joiningDate": "2024-04-01T00:00:00Z"
}

###

### 20. Forbidden Request — Standard User tries to DELETE Admin-only endpoint (Expected: 403 Forbidden)
DELETE {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.token}}

###

### 21. Authorized Admin Request — Admin deletes employee (Expected: 204 No Content or 404)
DELETE {{EmployeeManagement.API_HostAddress}}/api/employee/1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}
